spec dd08-ddl-on-one-object: 4 sessions, 24 permutations
# DD08. Four autocommit DDL statements on two objects: s1 creates index l_s, s2 drops
# it, s3 creates UNIQUE constraint c1 on (:K).k, s4 creates a constraint with the same
# name on (:K).v. Every order leaves a consistent catalog, and a DDL that cannot apply
# fails with an error that names why. The harness runs one step at a time, so the
# statements are serialised by the script; their overlap is #2934's.

starting permutation: s1ix s2drop s3c s4c
step s1ix: CREATE INDEX l_s FOR (n:L) ON (n.s)
step s2drop: DROP INDEX l_s
step s3c: CREATE CONSTRAINT c1 FOR (n:K) REQUIRE n.k IS UNIQUE
step s4c: CREATE CONSTRAINT c1 FOR (n:K) REQUIRE n.v IS UNIQUE
ERROR: cypher: cannot create constraint "c1": exec: constraint name already in use: name is already used by the UNIQUE constraint on (:K).k
final fschema: <schema>
kind      |name       |definition   
----------+-----------+-------------
index     |__uniq__K.k|             
constraint|c1         |UNIQUE (:K).k
(2 rows)

